{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghNhn5CiyyeTjapYonQv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For octahedral d², the three spin-allowed bands come from the ground term ³T₁g(F):\n\n- ν₁ = ³T₁g(F) → ³T₂g = 20 700 cm⁻¹\n- ν₂ = ³T₁g(F) → ³T₁g(P) = 30 570 cm⁻¹\n- ν₃ = ³T₁g(F) → ³A₂g = 42 990 cm⁻¹\n\n**Energy expressions (weak-field basis)**\n- ³T₂g sits at +2Dq and ³A₂g at +12Dq. Neither has another state of the same symmetry to mix with.\n- The two ³T₁g states mix. Their 2×2 matrix has diagonal elements −6Dq for ³T₁g(F) and 15B for ³T₁g(P), and off-diagonal element 4Dq.\n- So the two ³T₁g energies add up to 15B − 6Dq (the trace) and multiply to −90B·Dq − 16Dq² (the determinant).\n\n**1. Find Dq**\nThe ground-state energy cancels when you subtract ν₁ from ν₃:\nν₃ − ν₁ = 12Dq − 2Dq = 10Dq = 42 990 − 20 700 = 22 290 cm⁻¹\nSo **Dq = 2229 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**2. Find B**\n- Ground-state energy: E[³T₁g(F)] = 2Dq − ν₁ = 4458 − 20 700 = −16 242 cm⁻¹\n- Upper ³T₁g energy: E[³T₁g(P)] = E[³T₁g(F)] + ν₂ = −16 242 + 30 570 = 14 328 cm⁻¹\n- Sum of the two: −1914 = 15B − 6Dq = 15B − 13 374\n- So **B ≈ 761 cm⁻¹**.\n\n**Check with the determinant**\n- From the band energies: (−16 242)(14 328) ≈ −2.327 × 10⁸\n- From the fitted values: −90B·Dq − 16Dq² ≈ −2.321 × 10⁸\n- These agree to about 0.3%, so the band assignment holds together.\n\n**Result:** 10Dq ≈ 22 290 cm⁻¹ and B/Dq ≈ 0.34. B is about 761 cm⁻¹, which is lower than the free-ion value, as expected from the nephelauxetic effect. Spin-allowed bands alone don't give C, so it is left as null.\n\n{\"Dq\": 2229, \"B\": 761, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν3−ν1=10Dq and B from the 3T1g(F)/3T1g(P) secular equation trace.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1640,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1640,"ephemeral